{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonShift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonShift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.DiffContOnCl","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.ReImTopology"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.diffContOnCl_comp_add_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.diffContOnCl_comp_add_const","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelWatsonShift.lean#L43-L71","doc":"**The `DiffContOnCl` shift transport (boundary-argument crux).** If `f` is\nholomorphic on `{re > ε}` and continuous up to its closure `{re ≥ ε}`, then\nthe shifted `w ↦ f(w + ε)` is holomorphic on `{re > 0}` and continuous up to\n`{re ≥ 0}`. Both properties compose through the entire affine translation\n`w ↦ w + ε` (which maps `{re > 0} → {re > ε}` and `{re ≥ 0} → {re ≥ ε}`);\nthe closed half-planes are identified by `closure_setOf_lt_re`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}